===========================================================================
nm-freebsd has been installed.

Enable the daemon at boot:

    sysrc nm_freebsd_enable=YES

Start it now:

    service dbus restart
    service nm_freebsd start

KDE and GNOME need no extra UI. XFCE users can add "NetworkManager FreeBSD"
from the panel's "Add New Items" dialog after restarting xfce4-panel.

The D-Bus policy gives full control only to root and members of wheel or
network. Add a desktop user who is not in wheel:

    pw groupmod network -m <user>

then log out and back in. Do not install this MVP on a multi-user or hostile
local-user machine until polkit/SecretAgent support lands. Saved Wi-Fi
passwords are in /var/db/nm-freebsd/keyring.json (0600) and are not encrypted
at rest.

To let the daemon observe DHCP leases, add this line to
/etc/dhclient-exit-hooks (the one-click installer does it automatically):

    . %%PREFIX%%/libexec/nm-freebsd-dhcp-hook
===========================================================================
